Provenance
----------
The 12 operator modules in this repository were written to specifications
provided by the copyright holder, with implementation assistance from Google
Gemini. Adapted copies of some of these modules are maintained in the
hetero-moe research repository
(https://github.com/Microbiosis/hetero-moe) under
research/aligner/v62_dimension_projection_space/ and are distributed under
the same license.

Two files were changed on top of the shipped archive, in order to make the
package importable at all. Everything else is byte-identical to the archive:

  1. hybrid_moa_vl_operator_suite/__init__.py
     The shipped version imported 20 symbol names that do not exist in the
     modules (e.g. TritonKernelBenchmarkResult, NumpyQuantumTidalKernels,
     SupermembraneOperatorConfig, SpinalPathwayConfig, TulpaOperatorConfig,
     CorticospinalChaosConfig, BaryogenesisParityConfig, ...), so
     `import hybrid_moa_vl_operator_suite` raised ImportError. The imports and
     __all__ now use the names the modules actually define.

  2. hybrid_moa_vl_operator_suite/unified_hybrid_moa_architecture.py
     The shipped version used bare module imports (`from moa_operators import
     ...`) inside `try: import torch ... except ImportError: HAS_TORCH = False`.
     Loaded as a package those bare imports fail, so the ImportError was
     swallowed and the entire torch layer (UnifiedInterdisciplinaryMoALayer)
     was silently disabled. Imports are now dual-mode: package-relative first,
     plain module path when the file is executed directly
     (`python3 unified_hybrid_moa_architecture.py`). The sys.path manipulation
     that used to sit at the top of the file was removed.

Per-module license headers were deliberately not inserted, so the operator
files stay byte-identical to the archive apart from the two fixes above; the
repository-level LICENSE file applies to every file here.

smoke_test.py, README.md, NOTICE and .gitignore were written for this
repository and are likewise covered by the LICENSE file.

